Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Take the sink from the connector

dw-hdmi sets sink_is_hdmi and sink_has_audio only in its own EDID read
over DDC. An EDID override, or any EDID the connector has that DDC did
not give, never reaches them: with no screen on the bus the sink stays
DVI, and DVI mode sends no AVI, vendor or DRM InfoFrame at all, so an
HDR mode set on a synthetic HDR screen sends SDR.

Take both from the connector's display_info when the bridge is enabled,
as the FIXME beside the DDC read asks; it holds what the connector read,
the override included.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -3163,6 +3163,9 @@
 	mutex_lock(&hdmi->mutex);
 	hdmi->disabled = false;
 	hdmi->curr_conn = connector;
+	/* what the connector read, its EDID override too, not only our own DDC read */
+	hdmi->sink_is_hdmi = connector->display_info.is_hdmi;
+	hdmi->sink_has_audio = connector->display_info.has_audio;
 	dw_hdmi_update_power(hdmi);
 	dw_hdmi_update_phy_mask(hdmi);
 	handle_plugged_change(hdmi, true);
